# CREDITS — third-party assets

## nmf_fly.glb — NeuroMechFly 2.0 adult fruit-fly morphology (TrueFly-glb button)

- **Citation:** Wang-Chen, A. et al. *NeuroMechFly 2.0, a framework for
  simulating embodied sensorimotor control in adult Drosophila.* Nature
  (2025), https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-025-09029-4 (preprint: bioRxiv
  2023.09.18.556649).
- **Asset source:** MuJoCo MJCF body model (`fruitfly.xml`) + 85 body-segment
  OBJ meshes as published by the NeuroMechFly 2.0 / flybody project —
  https://github.com/NeLy-EPFL/flygym (assets under
  `src/flygym/assets/model/flybody/`; identical copies shipped in the
  `flybody==0.1.0` pip package at
  `.venv-embodiment/Lib/site-packages/flybody/fruitfly/assets/`, from which
  this build reads them). No assets were fabricated; no meshes were
  decimated (the packer is lossless OBJ→GLB).
- **License:** Apache License 2.0 (flygym repo `LICENSE`; flybody PyPI
  metadata "License: Apache License" — copies at
  `research_data/nmf_assets/LICENSE_flygym` and the package dist-info
  METADATA).
- **Build pipeline (render-only, offline):** `node tools/build_nmf_fly_glb.js`
  parses the MJCF `<body>` tree (joint pivots pos/quat per node, geoms with
  local pos/quat + material) and packs each referenced OBJ into a glTF 2.0
  binary scene: 151 nodes, 84 meshes, 270,734 triangles, 8 materials.
  MuJoCo default mesh scale 0.1 applied; units meters→scene handled by the
  runtime normalization (wingspan → 170 world units, matching the avatar it
  replaces; scale factor printed to console at load).
- **Runtime use:** fly_demon_3d.html TrueFly-glb button (render-only);
  `?fly=legacy` renders the previous Sketchfab fly (CC-BY-4.0, author
  victorberdugo1, https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/fly-6a4470f884554864827d848718b2b6bc)
  for side-by-side comparison and zero-code rollback. This mode changes
  nothing in simulation, physics, learning, or exports.

